---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const guide =
  'https://github.com/groovemap-music/deployment/blob/main/docs/homelab.md';
const repository = 'https://github.com/groovemap-music/deployment';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Run GrooveMap in your homelab"
  description="See what it takes to self-host GrooveMap on your own Docker host, and follow the homelab guide or let an AI agent set it up."
  path="/self-host/"
>
  <article class="article shell">
    <header class="article-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Self-host GrooveMap</p>
      <h1>Run GrooveMap in your homelab.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        GrooveMap is a self-hosted music knowledge graph built from the Discogs
        and MusicBrainz datasets. If you have a Docker host with room to spare,
        you can run your own copy.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="article-grid">
      <section aria-labelledby="involves-heading">
        <h2 id="involves-heading">What it involves</h2>
        <ul class="requirements">
          <li>
            <strong>A Docker host.</strong> Docker Engine with Docker Compose
            v2.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>An amd64 machine.</strong> The images are built for
            <code>linux/amd64</code> only.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Memory and disk.</strong> Plan on a machine in the 16 GB of
            memory and 100 GB of free disk class, with more recommended. The
            guide has the current numbers.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Patience on the first load.</strong> Importing the datasets
            takes hours, up to about two days. It can be interrupted and
            resumed.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby="paths-heading">
        <h2 id="paths-heading">Two ways to start</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>One command.</strong> The deployment repository checks your
          host, sets up configuration and secrets, starts the stack, and prints
          your URLs when the import is done.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Let an AI agent do it.</strong> In Claude Code, the
          <code>groovemap-homelab</code> plugin fits GrooveMap into your reverse
          proxy, storage, and ports. Add it with
          <code>/plugin marketplace add groovemap-music/deployment</code>, then
          <code>/plugin install groovemap-homelab@groovemap</code>.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby="guide-heading">
        <h2 id="guide-heading">Read the guide first</h2>
        <p>
          The homelab guide is the source of truth for sizing, ports, reverse
          proxies, upgrades, and known limitations. Check it before you commit a
          machine to the first load.
        </p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button primary" href={guide}>
            Read the homelab guide
          </a>
          <a class="button secondary" href={repository}>
            Open the deployment repository
          </a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
